# Build output
/bin/
/dist/
# `go build ./...` drops each command binary in the working directory
/bot

# Local environment — the bot token and DSN never enter the repository
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Scratch. Every gate log, mutation backup and throwaway probe a flow writes
# lands here — capture to a file, never pipe a gate.
# One ignored directory instead of a spreading pattern: 60 `*.gate.log` files
# had accumulated in the repository root by 2026-09-05, invisible to
# `git status` and therefore to everyone, because the ignore rule was a glob
# over a filename the canonical command never fixed.
/tmp/

# Retired run state. A flow COMMITS its progress and interview-state files while
# it runs (so a delegate's truncating edit is recoverable from history), then
# `mv`s them here and commits the deletion of the old paths as the last commit
# before the PR. Ignoring the directory keeps them out of the repo; moving them
# also takes them out of the equivalent progress-file and spec-state-file
# probes, which a plain untrack does not.
/ai-docs/plans/ignored/
/ai-docs/main-ci/ignored/

# Harness local-only state
/ai-docs/plans/**/*.progress.md
# /task in-flight marker (Stop-hook contract)
/ai-docs/plans/.task-inflight
/ai-docs/pr-comments/
/ai-docs/bugfix/trace-*.md
/ai-docs/triage/*.progress.md

# Per-machine / local settings
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# IDE
/.idea/

# pgregory.net/rapid writes a timestamped .fail file here on every property failure;
# a defect worth keeping becomes a table-test case, never a checked-in fail file
**/testdata/rapid/
